    {
      "id": "10c360f6-b83b-4205-8e46-f4382f66680c",
      "patientId": "p-d5569845",
      "from": "user",
      "text": "I am feeling pain in my stomach",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T15:36:57.877Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1da43e3-5d45-4978-98b8-1228a004cb00",
      "patientId": "p-d5569845",
      "from": "vita",
      "text": "I'm sorry to hear you're feeling pain in your stomach. As a health companion, I can't diagnose what's causing it, but gathering more details can be helpful.\n\nCould you tell me a little more about the pain?\n*   Where exactly is the pain located in your stomach area?\n*   How would you describe the pain (e.g., sharp, dull, cramping, burning)?\n*   When did it start, and has it been constant or does it come and go?\n*   Are you experiencing any other symptoms, like fever, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, or changes in your appetite?\n\nIf the pain is sudden and very severe, or if you also have trouble breathing, severe vomiting, or are feeling faint, please contact emergency services immediately.\n\nFor a proper check-up and advice tailored to you, I would recommend visiting our clinic. They can assess your symptoms directly.",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T15:37:01.768Z"
    }
